 This story taught people not to be greedy. This story reminded people to avoid greed.", "Oral heritage. Stories passed practices and beliefs between generations. Moral stories were used for education, rather than as historical records."], "text": "Several forms. Pantun, syair and proverbs conveyed lessons. These forms of language made advice memorable. Community advice. Sayings and taboos guided behaviour. Lessons were passed down through different means of communication. Si Tanggang. This story warned children against being disobedient to their parents. The key value was respect for one’s parents. The Dog and Its Reflection. This story taught people not to be greedy. This story reminded people to avoid greed. Oral heritage. Stories passed practices and beliefs between generations. Moral stories were used for education, rather than as historical records."}